+// what IOSurfaceIsInUse() reports. Chromium's swap-chain, CVPixelBufferPool (VideoToolbox decoder output) and Core Animation
+// only recycle a surface - write the next frame into it - once it is no longer in use. Without it WindowServer's GPU could
+// still be compositing a surface the app was already redrawing: diagonally torn windows while resizing/scrolling, video
+// frames overwritten under the reader. A texture's command-buffer references (_resRefs, released when the GPU work
